<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    <title>Welcome, <%= name %></title>
    <%- include('partials/acct-head') %>
</head>
<body>
<header class="bar">
    <div class="wrap">
        <a class="mark" href="/">
            <span class="mark-dots" aria-hidden="true"><i style="background:var(--c-red)"></i><i style="background:var(--c-yellow)"></i><i style="background:var(--c-blue)"></i><i style="background:var(--c-green)"></i><i style="background:var(--c-purple)"></i><i style="background:var(--c-pink)"></i></span>
            Password Strength Enhancement
        </a>
        <div class="who"><span><%= email %></span></div>
    </div>
</header>

<main class="wrap">
    <section class="top">
        <div>
            <h1>Welcome, <%= name %>. Your account is ready.</h1>
            <p>Your password is saved with its colours, so it is harder to guess than the same letters in plain text. This is its shape.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
            <%- include('partials/strip', {pw: pw}) %>
            <p class="strip-cap"><%= pw.length %> characters, <%= pw.colouredCount %> coloured. Dashed circles have no colour.</p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="block">
        <div>
            <h2>Before you log in</h2>
            <p class="why">Three things to remember about a colour password.</p>
        </div>
        <ol class="notes">
            <li>
                <h3>Type the same characters</h3>
                <p>Enter your email, then your password exactly as you chose it.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
                <h3>Paint the same colours</h3>
                <p>Select the same characters and apply the same colours. The right letters with the wrong colours will not log you in.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
                <h3>Take a picture of the pattern</h3>
                <p>The colours are easy to forget if you only remember the word. Write down which characters were which colour, somewhere private.</p>
            </li>
        </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="block">
        <div>
            <h2>Your strength estimate</h2>
            <p class="why">Colour adds guesses an attacker has to make, on top of the characters.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
            <div class="score"><strong><%= pw.total %></strong><span>bits, rated <em><%= pw.rating %></em></span></div>
            <% var pct1 = pw.total ? Math.round(pw.base / pw.total * 100) : 100; %>
            <div class="bar-split" role="img" aria-label="<%= pw.base %> bits from characters, <%= pw.bonus %> bits from colour"><i class="b1" style="width:<%= pct1 %>%"></i><i class="b2" style="width:<%= 100 - pct1 %>%"></i></div>
            <ul class="legend">
                <li><b><%= pw.base %></b> bits from characters</li>
                <li><b>+<%= pw.bonus %></b> bits from colour</li>
            </ul>
            <a class="go" href="/homepage">Log in</a>
        </div>
    </section>

    <footer class="foot">Prototype. Strength figures are rough estimates, not a guarantee.</footer>
</main>
</body>
</html>
